---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/site/FinalCta.astro';
const rows = [
  [
    'Getting started',
    'Choose your own format and fill every field.',
    'Open it and start logging. No account required.',
  ],
  ['An everyday dish', 'Write a name, then look up its parts.', 'Start from one transparent ingredient composition.'],
  ['Photo logging', 'Describe the meal yourself.', 'Review a simulated sample mapping; no actual recognition.'],
  [
    'Nutrition arithmetic',
    'Find values, scale grams and add totals.',
    'Source records and serving math stay linked to entries.',
  ],
  [
    'Packaged food',
    'Copy the label or find a product elsewhere.',
    'Look up complete Open Food Facts records by barcode.',
  ],
  ['Keeping a copy', 'Keep your chosen file or notebook.', 'Export JSON; local browser storage can be cleared.'],
  ['Flexibility', 'Completely open-ended.', 'Four meal groups, core macros and a curated starting set.'],
];
---

<SiteLayout title="A place to begin" description="An honest comparison between Busog and a blank food diary."
  ><section class="page-intro">
    <p class="mono">Busog vs a blank food diary</p><h1>A place to begin.<br />Room to make it yours.</h1><p>
      A blank page is wonderfully flexible. Busog adds a few useful starting points, with the limits in view.
    </p>
  </section><div class="table-wrap comparison">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>At the table</th><th>A blank diary</th><th>Busog</th></tr></thead><tbody
        >{
          rows.map(([name, blank, busog]) => (
            <tr>
              <>
                <th>{name}</th>
                <td>{blank}</td>
                <td>{busog}</td>
              </>
            </tr>
          ))
        }</tbody
      >
    </table>
  </div><article class="reading">
    <h2>Choose what helps you.</h2><p>
      A notebook does not need a battery, API or browser cache. It also does not calculate nutrition for you. Busog is a
      different tool: explicit compositions, sourced numbers and a focused set of features.
    </p><p>
      We haven't benchmarked Busog against other trackers for accuracy, speed or outcomes, so you won't find competitor
      claims or performance statistics here.
    </p>
  </article><FinalCta /></SiteLayout
>
<style>
  .comparison {
    border-radius: 28px;
    background: var(--raised);
  }
  .comparison th:first-child {
    min-width: 140px;
  }
  .comparison td {
    min-width: 220px;
    width: 37%;
  }
  .comparison td:last-child,
  .comparison th:last-child {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, var(--raised));
  }
</style>
